## Next

1. Let NAFNet and tone-safe Restormer continue running overnight unless GPU scheduling changes.
2. When tone-safe Restormer reaches epoch 3, run the same 42-frame probe and compare against the earlier Restormer E3 result.
3. Key Restormer pass criterion: `dY` within about `-5` at minimum, preferably near `-2 ~ +2`, while preserving meaningful noise suppression.
4. Keep Deploy as production baseline/guardrail, not the preferred Teacher if NAFNet detail preservation remains visually superior.
5. Prepare MTKD only after at least one Teacher candidate passes tone/detail/noise gates on real MC-G105 captures.
